@startuml
' Source (synthetic brief): the bookshop's web orders on AWS, in five numbered steps. 1. A customer
' places an order through the web shop (API Gateway). 2. An order Lambda saves the order in DynamoDB.
' 3. The Lambda publishes an OrderPlaced event to an SQS queue. 4. A fulfilment Lambda reads the queue
' and writes a packing slip to S3. 5. The shop manager reads the daily slips from S3.
' Not stated: retries and the dead-letter queue.
' house-preamble-begin
' Knob LEGEND_FRAME: colour of the thin frame around the legend ("transparent" removes it).
!$LEGEND_FRAME = "#999999"
!theme plain
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam wrapWidth 300
skinparam maxMessageSize 300
skinparam legendBackgroundColor transparent
skinparam legendBorderColor $LEGEND_FRAME
skinparam nodesep 40
skinparam ranksep 50
hide stereotype
<style>
root { FontName "Helvetica"; FontSize 12 }
title { FontSize 16 }
</style>
!include <awslib20/AWSCommon>
!include <awslib20/Groups/AWSCloud>
!include <awslib20/Groups/Generic>
!include <awslib20/Groups/Region>
!include <awslib20/Groups/VPC>
!include <awslib20/Groups/AvailabilityZone>
!include <awslib20/Groups/PublicSubnet>
!include <awslib20/Groups/PrivateSubnet>
!include <awslib20/Groups/AutoScalingGroup>
' Numbered steps (optional, STYLE rule 16): $step(1) prints a blue badge in a label, an edge label
' or a legend table row. Knob STEP_BADGE: the badge colour.
!$STEP_BADGE = "#1565C0"
!function $step($n)
!return "<back:" + $STEP_BADGE + "><color:#FFFFFF><b> " + $n + " </b></color></back>"
!endfunction
' house-preamble-end
!include <awslib20/General/Users>
!include <awslib20/NetworkingContentDelivery/APIGateway>
!include <awslib20/Compute/Lambda>
!include <awslib20/Database/DynamoDB>
!include <awslib20/ApplicationIntegration/SimpleQueueService>
!include <awslib20/Storage/SimpleStorageService>

skinparam nodesep 110
skinparam ranksep 100
title Container diagram for the bookshop web orders on AWS, in five steps (synthetic)

Users(customer, "Customer", "browser")
AWSCloudGroup(cloud, "AWS Cloud") {
  APIGateway(api, "Web shop API", "Amazon API Gateway")
  Lambda(order_fn, "Order handler", "AWS Lambda")
  DynamoDB(orders, "Orders", "Amazon DynamoDB")
  SimpleQueueService(queue, "Order events", "Amazon SQS")
  Lambda(pack_fn, "Fulfilment", "AWS Lambda")
  SimpleStorageService(slips, "Packing slips", "Amazon S3")
}
Users(manager, "Shop manager", "browser")

customer -right-> api : $step(1) orders\n(HTTPS)
api -down-> order_fn : invokes\n(Lambda)
order_fn -right-> orders : $step(2) saves\n(DynamoDB API)
order_fn -down-> queue : $step(3) publishes\n(SQS)
queue -right-> pack_fn : $step(4) delivers\n(SQS poll)
pack_fn -down-> slips : writes slip\n(S3 PUT)
manager -up-> slips : $step(5) reads slips\n(HTTPS)

legend bottom
  |= Step |= What happens |
  | $step(1) | a customer places an order in the web shop |
  | $step(2) | the order handler saves it in DynamoDB |
  | $step(3) | it publishes OrderPlaced to the queue |
  | $step(4) | the fulfilment function writes a packing slip to S3 |
  | $step(5) | the shop manager reads the day's slips |
  |= Mark |= Meaning |
  | icon | AWS service named in the source (official AWS icon) |
  | AWS Cloud frame | the services the source places on AWS |
endlegend
@enduml
